<h2>Search Bar (FireSearch)</h2>

<p>
    The search bar at the top of the screen is your fastest way to navigate Quickfire. It's called "FireSearch" and it can find almost anything:
</p>

<ul>
    <li><strong>Clients</strong> – Search by company name, contact name, or lookup code</li>
    <li><strong>Policies</strong> – Find policies by number, client, or carrier</li>
    <li><strong>Carriers</strong> – Search for insurance companies</li>
    <li><strong>Documents</strong> – Find files, forms, and attachments</li>
    <li><strong>Renewals</strong> – Search for specific renewals</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>Keyboard shortcuts:</strong>
</p>

<ul>
    <li>Press <strong>/</strong> (forward slash) to quickly focus the search bar from anywhere</li>
    <li>Use <strong>Arrow keys</strong> to move through search results</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Enter</strong> to open the selected result</li>
    <li>Press <strong>Ctrl+Enter</strong> to open the result in a new tab</li>
</ul>

<p>
    The search bar learns as you use it, so frequently accessed items appear first. It's the fastest way to jump to any client, policy, or record without clicking through menus.
</p>

